    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Rufmariasch',
            subtitle: 'Card game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Rufmariasch is an Austrian four-player Mariage variant. 32-card German pack (hearts, bells, acorns, leaves). Bidder calls a card (Ace or King) to choose partner. Aces, tens, last trick = 10 pts. King+Over (Queen) = mariage: 40 trumps, 20 other. Point-trick with called partner.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Rufmariasch is a Danube Swabian variant of Mariáš for four players, played by the Donauschwaben (German settlers on the Danube) in 18th- and 19th-century Hungary. It belongs to the Mariage (king-queen) family of ace-ten games; the name combines the French mariage with German rufen (to call). It uses a 32-card William Tell pack and variable partnerships chosen by calling a card.',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '4 in temporary partnerships.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32 German (A-10-K-O-U-9-8-7).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '32-card German pack.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Dealer shuffles and the player to dealer's right cuts. The dealer deals four cards to each player and pauses. The player to dealer's left (forehand) calls a card by rank and suit; that suit becomes trumps and the holder is the caller's partner. The dealer then deals a second batch of four cards to each player so everyone has eight cards.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'MariÃ¡Å¡: Czech variant.',
                  },
                ],
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
